def reverse_words(s: str) -> str:
    """Reverse word order in a single-space-delimited string."""
    if not s:
        return ""
    chars = list(s)
    def reverse_range(lo: int, hi: int) -> None:
        while lo < hi:
            chars[lo], chars[hi] = chars[hi], chars[lo]
            lo += 1
            hi -= 1
    reverse_range(0, len(chars) - 1)
    start = 0
    for i, ch in enumerate(chars):
        if ch == ' ':
            reverse_range(start, i - 1)
            start = i + 1
    reverse_range(start, len(chars) - 1)
    return ''.join(chars)
```
Reverses the whole char array, then reverses each word in place. Two passes, O(n) time, O(n) space for the char list.

