from collections import Counter

def are_anagrams(a: str, b: str) -> bool:
    if len(a) != len(b):
        return False
    return Counter(a) == Counter(b)
```
Uses Counter for clean, readable frequency comparison. Early length check avoids unnecessary work. Pythonic and efficient!

